# Starfleet Communicator {3} is copied as it is cast, so a token copy of the Equipment enters beside the original
# (CR 707.10f). With a Communicator on each of three attacking-capable 0/2 Ornithopters, attacking with one of them makes X
# the number of *other* creatures with a Communicator attached - the two it left behind, not the attacker itself, and not
# Bot2's equipped Ornithopter - so the attack draws two cards and may put up to two lands from hand onto the battlefield
# tapped (CR 608.2c, 608.2d, 614.1c). The two cards drawn on turn 7 are both lands and both are put, which is why a count of
# one fails; the Forest played this turn leaves no other land in hand, so the empty hand is exactly two drawn. On turn 9 the
# same attack declines the up-to-two, and the two lands it drew stay in hand.

